{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/836675-changing-tribe-totems","id":836675,"title":"Changing Tribe Totems","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-24T14:14:47-08:00","id":836675,"title":"Changing Tribe Totems","content":"I'm doing this to put out ideas on changing what tribes have what totems. The reason why is because when you actually put thought into it, the totems of a number of tribes don't make sense or White Wolf used some pretty absurd justifications for them.<br /> -Black Furies should not have Pegasus as a totem. Pegasus is a male and was conceived through rape and was born from the murder of Medusa. Aspects of that can be argued about why the Furies would or would not serve Pegasus but I'm not trying to get into that. My suggestion is instead give them Owl. In mythology the owl was the sacred animal of Athena which I think would be a good fit for the Furies.<br /> -Bone Gnawers I haven't got to yet, probably would keep their totem<br /> -Children of Gaia I also haven't got to yet<br /> -Fianna have Stag which seems appropriate, at least for the time<br /> -Get of Fenris are kind of ok<br /> -Glass Walker I haven't thought too much on<br /> -Red Talons I don't think should have Griffon for a couple reasons, one of which is they are species purists and Griffon is a mix of two animals, another is I think Griffon might be better for the Silver Fang, see below<br /> -Shadow Lords are great with Grandfather Thunder<br /> -Silent Striders wouldn't have owl anymore and I don't think it was too appropriate anyway, instead they should have Jackal for several reasons, some less obvious than others<br /> -Silver Fangs have Falcon which I'm not against but I think Griffon would be better, not how crazy Griffon is currently written but as he is a symbol of as part king of the sky and predator king.<br /> -Uktena and Wendigo I'm not getting into, at least for now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T15:09:01-08:00","id":836700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/836675-changing-tribe-totems#post836675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm doing this to put out ideas on changing what tribes have what totems. The reason why is because when you actually put thought into it, the totems of a number of tribes don't make sense or White Wolf used some pretty absurd justifications for them.<br /> -Black Furies should not have Pegasus as a totem. Pegasus is a male and was conceived through rape and was born from the murder of Medusa. Aspects of that can be argued about why the Furies would or would not serve Pegasus but I'm not trying to get into that. My suggestion is instead give them Owl. In mythology the owl was the sacred animal of Athena which I think would be a good fit for the Furies.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Furies hate Athena something fierce, though, on account of her eschewing femininity, and being the namesake/sponsor one of the few Grecian city-states that could make Sparta look progressive. Meanwhile, Pegasus was utterly screwed over by Bellerophon, which included being gelded, and so there's fellow victim sympathy there.<br /> <br /> Then again, it would also be somewhat refreshing to move the Furies away from GREECEGREECEGREECEGREECE, particularly because, in being inspired by legends of Amazons, they're being inspired by figures of Greek legendry that were not Greek. The Amazons were foreigners to the people telling the tales. There could be room for a more general &quot;heavenly horse&quot; as a totem, though, which could expand their range considerably.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Get of Fenris are kind of ok </div> </div> </div>It's kind of the core thesis of the tribe above and beyond any others, really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Red Talons I don't think should have Griffon for a couple reasons, one of which is they are species purists and Griffon is a mix of two animals, another is I think Griffon might be better for the Silver Fang, see below </div> </div> </div>I can recall nothing about Red Talons being freaked out by spirits that are part of a bunch of different animals. The main bit that could be emphasized better is in turn mythology on its head. Griffin guards treasure, it's said; humans think it means gold, but the Red Talons know it means vibrant, healthy wilderness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Silent Striders wouldn't have owl anymore and I don't think it was too appropriate anyway, instead they should have Jackal for several reasons, some less obvious than others </div> </div> </div>They're associated with death. Owl tends to weigh that way more often than as a symbol of wisdom, once you get outside of Europe. The Striders also tend to be loners more often than jackals are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Silver Fangs have Falcon which I'm not against but I think Griffon would be better, not how crazy Griffon is currently written but as he is a symbol of as part king of the sky and predator king. </div> </div> </div>There's an elaborate story about Wolf and the Darkness that I could never bring myself to scrap to go along with Falcon and the Silver Fangs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 02-24-2016, 08:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T15:35:46-08:00","id":836713,"title":"","content":"If we're going to redo the Tribal Totems, I'd rather move away from the (mainly) animal/mythological creature approach to them. <br /> <br /> I'd rather see far more conceptual Totems, which could have many in-character names/avatars, with the animal/myths/personifications being highly associated with the Tribes because of their associations with those concepts. This also allows a lot more focus on the themes of the Tribe over the cultural stereotypes of them.<br /> <br /> As an example, the Glasswalkers could follow Techne (cribbing that from recent musing about MtAw 2e). Techne is the spirit of technological innovation, that exists in an odd balance between the Wyld and Weaver. Techne is somewhat fickle, not caring about either the long traditions of ancient crafting techniques or the ethical ramifications of creativity. Instead Techne is the patron of inspired genius that pushes boundaries and creates new inventions for all. Cockroach, and her brood, is a favored lieutenant to Techne. Few animal spirits can keep up with the rapid adaptation Techne inspires, while being bound to the human world of technology and science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T16:13:40-08:00","id":836728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/836675-changing-tribe-totems?p=836700#post836700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Furies hate Athena something fierce, though, on account of her eschewing femininity, and being the namesake/sponsor one of the few Grecian city-states that could make Sparta look progressive. Meanwhile, Pegasus was utterly screwed over by Bellerophon, which included being gelded, and so there's fellow victim sympathy there.<br /> <br /> Then again, it would also be somewhat refreshing to move the Furies away from GREECEGREECEGREECEGREECE, particularly because, in being inspired by legends of Amazons, they're being inspired by figures of Greek legendry that were not Greek. The Amazons were foreigners to the people telling the tales. There could be room for a more general &quot;heavenly horse&quot; as a totem, though, which could expand their range considerably.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Also, wasn't it Athena who punished Medusa for the crime of being raped? Not exactly Fury friendly either....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T17:10:29-08:00","id":836754,"title":"","content":"Depends which version of the mythology you're using.<br /> <br /> It's most likely that Athena victim-cursing Medusa was actually a later addition to the story, meaning that the Furies could easily see it as men rewriting the &quot;truth&quot; to perpetuate patriarchal revisions. In the oldest versions, all of the Gorgons were presented as born monsters, with Medusa just being the least monstrous of them (or able to pass as human more easily, or something, it's pretty vague stuff). Medusa seemed to get &quot;prettier&quot; as time went on... until Ovid wrote the version we're most familiar with down where she was born stunningly beautiful, only to be raped by Poseidon in Athena's temple, and getting cursed by Athena for it (including Ovid writing it as an explicit statement that she got &quot;what she deserved&quot;).<br /> <br /> While the Furies might not like Athena, they probably don't like a myth being twisted by rich men to include a, &quot;beautiful women deserve to be raped for being so good looking men can't resist it,&quot; aside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T05:21:08-08:00","id":836979,"title":"","content":"Isn't the Pegasus Totem female?<br /> <br /> I wouldn't go with Jackal, they are very clearly steering clear of Canines as Tribal totems besides Fenris.<br /> <br /> Two of the Three Brothers from the Purelands have different Totems. Uktena used to have that Skyhawk as their Totem, and Wendigo used to be Sasquatch the same spirit but it changed after the Iceage.<br /> <br /> Maybe give the Warders of Man the Wheel as a totem, or Prometheus/Sacred Fire","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T09:21:13-08:00","id":837055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/836675-changing-tribe-totems?p=836979#post836979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't the Pegasus Totem female?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't have the tribebook to confirm, but a friend of mine told me that Pegasus was castrated in the backstory for the book, likely because someone realized &quot;oh shit, we have our feminist tribe worshiping a male spirit&quot;<br /> <br /> As far as the responses from my original post go, I made that post in the same half hour I had the idea and haven't fully thought out possible replacements. The thing is, the ones whitewolf gave don't fit well. I forgot about the dislike for Athena stuff, but then how about some association with Artemis? You are right about the fact that they need to get out of the Greek obsession considering yes, they were invaders of Greece, not Greek themselves. The Red Talon species purity thing I mentioned was their own, they hate anything to do with humans and their own human halves, while Griffin is a mix of two different species. As far as going with the treasure protection thing, I think that works just as well for Silver Fangs plus my original stuff I said about being made of two great species. I do concede the Owl point though completely.<br /> <br /> I think the ideas involving getting away from animals both mythological and real and into the more esoteric totems is a great idea that probably fits the themes of Werewolf even more. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T18:09:34-08:00","id":837327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/836675-changing-tribe-totems?p=837055#post837055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't have the tribebook to confirm, but a friend of mine told me that Pegasus was castrated in the backstory for the book, likely because someone realized &quot;oh shit, we have our feminist tribe worshiping a male spirit&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it probably had more to do with a relation to Medusa, since the Gorgons are protrayed as being the first of the tribe (and increased in number to five).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As far as the responses from my original post go, I made that post in the same half hour I had the idea and haven't fully thought out possible replacements. The thing is, the ones whitewolf gave don't fit well. I forgot about the dislike for Athena stuff, but then how about some association with Artemis? </div> </div> </div>Artemis is usually only a figure for much angrier Furies that live away from civilization. It's why the rite that tears away the Veil from a single human is sometimes known as Actaeon's Folly. That could certainly use some tuning up, but by and large, the main figures of Greek myth tied into Fury culture are the Gorgons and the Erinys.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Red Talon species purity thing I mentioned was their own, they hate anything to do with humans and their own human halves, while Griffin is a mix of two different species. </div> </div> </div>Neither of which is human, so I'm still at a loss to understand what you think they have against it. They hate humans, go out of their way to kill humans, and avoid humans, not chimerae.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As far as going with the treasure protection thing, I think that works just as well for Silver Fangs plus my original stuff I said about being made of two great species. </div> </div> </div>Which would be odd for a tribe that actually shies away from outbreeding. Besides, you could also tie in falconry as practiced by aristocrats as a perversion of the veneration that the Fangs have for their totem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the ideas involving getting away from animals both mythological and real and into the more esoteric totems is a great idea that probably fits the themes of Werewolf even more. </div> </div> </div>I don't share that preference. The more abstract you get, the less visceral it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 02-25-2016, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T19:12:51-08:00","id":837353,"title":"","content":"I've gone back and forth on several of the tribal totems myself, but in all honesty, they are so tied up in the identity of the tribe that changing their totem would drastically change the tribe itself. Rather than taking the human mythology literally, it's better to find connections between what the stories may represent and what the Garou believe, or what the Garou know from the spirit world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7445-viking-funeral","name":"Viking Funeral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7445_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T23:42:35-08:00","id":837407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/836675-changing-tribe-totems?p=836979#post836979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe give the Warders of Man the Wheel as a totem, or Prometheus/Sacred Fire</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Glass Walkers have changed Tribal Totems over the years depending on which camp dominates the Tribe for a long time. So this would fit in line.<br /> <br /> For example, the Tribal Totem for the Iron Riders (<i>Wild West</i>) was Stourbridge Lion.<br /> It's never stated what totem the Tetrasomnians (<i>Italian Renaissance</i>) followed, though. Considering that they were alchemists, some aspect of Mitanu (<i>Mercury</i>), might work.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> Also, Uktena establishing a foothold in Europe might encounter Tatzelwurm, a cousin totem to Uktena that is re-discovered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","user":"Laughing Hyena","date":". 02-26-2016, 02:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}